  ⚠ typescript(adjacent-overload-signatures): All "\\uD800" signatures should be adjacent.
   ╭─[adjacent_overload_signatures.tsx:1:15]
 1 │ interface I { "\uD800"(): void; normal(): void; "\ud800"(x: number): void; }
   ·               ────────                          ────────
   ╰────
  help: Move all "\\uD800" overload signatures together, placing them consecutively before any other members.
  note: Function overload signatures represent multiple ways a function can be called. Keeping them adjacent makes it easier for developers to understand all available call signatures at a glance.

